// Title: Remote PowerShell Session Host Process (WinRM)
// Sigma ID: 734f8d9b-42b8-41b2-bcf5-abaf49d5a3c8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez @Cyb3rWard0g
// Date: 2019-09-12 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: execution, lateral-movement, T1059.001, T1021.006
// Description: Detects remote PowerShell sections by monitoring for wsmprovhost (WinRM host process) as a
//   parent or child process (sign of an active PowerShell remote session).
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of remote Powershell, e.g. for monitoring purposes.
// References:
//   - https://threathunterplaybook.com/hunts/windows/190511-RemotePwshExecution/notebook.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_winrm_remote_powershell_session_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\wsmprovhost.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\wsmprovhost.exe"
